.TH RICHCHAR 1 "August 2026" "Richchar 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
richchar \- local-first talking portrait generator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B richchar
--image IMAGE
(--text TEXT | --script-file FILE)
--voice-model MODEL
--output FILE
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Richchar orchestrates Piper text-to-speech, Wav2Lip GAN lip synchronization,
GFPGAN v1.4 face restoration, and FFmpeg encoding.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --image FILE
Source photographic portrait.
.TP
.B --text TEXT
Inline narration.
.TP
.B --script-file FILE
Read narration from a text file.
.TP
.B --voice-model FILE
Piper ONNX voice model.
.TP
.B --output FILE
Destination MP4.
.TP
.B --preview-seconds N
Limit processing to a short preview where supported.
.TP
.B --resume
Reuse completed intermediate work where supported.
.TP
.B --box TOP BOTTOM LEFT RIGHT
Supply a manual face region to Wav2Lip.
.TP
.B --doctor
Check local dependencies and configured model/runtime paths.
.TP
.B --help
Display command help.
.SH PIPELINE
Piper creates WAV audio. Wav2Lip GAN creates synchronized facial motion.
FFmpeg extracts lossless PNG frames. GFPGAN restores complete frames.
FFmpeg encodes H.264 output using the quality baseline.
.SH QUALITY BASELINE
Wav2Lip GAN uses --nosmooth. GFPGAN v1.4 uses upscale 1, clean architecture,
channel multiplier 2, center-face restoration, paste-back enabled and weight 0.65.
Final encoding uses libx264, CRF 14, preset slow and yuv420p.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
richchar --image portrait.png \\
  --text "Welcome to Richmack OS." \\
  --voice-model voice.onnx \\
  --output final.mp4
.fi
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Run `richchar --doctor` before troubleshooting a render.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Version 1.1.0 targets photographic human portraits. Cartoon and heavily
illustrated faces are not a validated quality target.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success. Non-zero indicates a validation, dependency,
rendering, restoration, encoding or filesystem failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ffmpeg (1),
.BR python3 (1)
